# - Stress errors are in meV per cubic Angstrom (no vocabulary unit; in the label, not converted). The HDNNP was not trained on stress. Some HDNNP rows have MAE above RMSE as printed (hot bulk 2 energy 3.59 / 3.68; defects energy 2.53 / 3.68), which cannot be right for one of the two numbers; to be checked against the PDF.
# - The per-group results all point at the one UO2 material node, with the group in the metric label; the groups are parts of the testing database, not separate materials.
# - The SNAP angular-momentum limit and the HDNNP symmetry-function set and cutoff are in the paper's ref. [48] and not encoded; the SNAP implementation (LAMMPS) is not in the vocabulary and is left out. Defect formation energies (Table II), gamma surfaces, polymorph equations of state and thermal properties are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

